<title>CANADA: Shell Canada to buy back 14 pct of shares.</title>
<headline>Shell Canada to buy back 14 pct of shares.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Canada Ltd said on Wednesday that it has offered to buy back 16 million or 14 percent of its class A common shares at a price of not more than C$61 a share and not less than C$53 a share.</p>
<p>The Calgary-based vertically integrated energy company said in a statement that the offer expires on May 26, unless it is extended and is subject to final regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>Shell said shareholders have a choice of participating either through an auction tender or proportionate tender, but not both.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
